 **Outputs:** A gradient vector field $\nabla V$, where each voxel $(i, j, k)$ has an associated 3D vector $(g_x, g_y, g_z)$ [S8, unofficial][S29, book].
 
 **Data Structures:**
-*   **Input Volume:** 1D array or 3D texture of scalar values $V_{i,j,k}$.
-*   **Output Gradient:** 1D array of size $W \times H \times D \times 3$ (interleaved RGB) or a 3D texture with 3 or 4 channels (e.g., RGBA8_SNORM) [S8, S17, unofficial].
